  <name>jellytoast</name>
  <summary>Audio-first music client for Jellyfin and Subsonic</summary>

  <description>
    <p>
      jellytoast is a native PySide6 desktop music client for Jellyfin
      and Subsonic / OpenSubsonic / Navidrome servers. Bit-perfect mpv
      playback, gapless audio, MPRIS2 system integration, system-tray
      controls, and a floating mini player.
    </p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Browse albums, artists, songs, playlists, and genres</li>
      <li>Bit-perfect mpv playback with optional server-side transcode tiers</li>
      <li>Gapless playback and ReplayGain (track / album)</li>
      <li>Chromecast and AirPlay 2 support, with a local relay for remote / Tailscale servers</li>
      <li>Explicit downloads with full offline playback (cascade by album / artist / playlist)</li>
      <li>Synced and plain lyrics, with a dedicated now-playing page</li>
      <li>Floating mini player with optional always-on-top (KDE Wayland)</li>
      <li>MPRIS2 + system-tray integration; media-key support</li>
    </ul>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.augustvontrips66.jellytoast.desktop</launchable>

